    "limitations": [
      "Quick-look visualization, not a significant motion or variability measurement.",
      "Each frame is the per-pixel median of up to 3 single exposures from one visit; the displayed time is the midpoint of the first and last exposure used. Changes within a visit are averaged away.",
      "Each exposure has its own median level subtracted, which removes background differences between visits and also any uniform extended emission. Values are raw DN without zero-point scaling; this is not photometry.",
      "No bad-pixel bitmask or uncertainty image is applied. The median rejects isolated artefacts, but diffraction spikes, latents, scattered moonlight and saturated cores remain.",
      "2 of the 6 visits found are sampled, evenly spaced through the eligible visits and including their first and last. Each requires the configured minimum exposure count. The others were not downloaded, so short-lived changes between frames are not shown.",
      "Alignment is WCS reprojection only; the stationary-source check labels frames and applies no correction.",
      "W2 is a broad filter (4.60 \u00b5m, 1.04 \u00b5m wide). It is not comparable with a SPHEREx spectral channel.",
      "PNG rows are flipped relative to FITS: fitsY=height-1-pngY (zero-based)."
    ],
